# Go build output
*.exe
*.exe~
/server/ags
/server/ags.exe

# Capture logs (regenerated at runtime)
/docs/capture.log
/docs/capture.log.prev
/docs/server.out.log
/server/docs/

# ags's own stdout/stderr redirects. Anchored to /server/ on purpose:
# docs/ags-*.log must stay trackable, because the sibling backend's captured
# stdout (docs/ds-server-*.log, 30 files) is tracked DELIBERATELY as route
# evidence and an unanchored `ags-*.log` would swallow the next one.
/server/ags-*.log

# Interactive (Track B) runtime player state
/server/state/
# ...and the same file when ags is started from the repo root instead:
# interactive.go's newStore("state/interactive.json") is CWD-relative, so the
# store lands wherever ags was launched from. Anchored rather than a bare
# `state/` so a future Go package at server/internal/state/ stays trackable.
/state/

# Live-process image dumps (usmapdump dumpimage) — hundreds of MB, regenerable
/dumps/

# Crashpad/Sentry minidumps — ~44 MB each. Every one on disk today already sits
# under /dumps/ or unreal-stub/Saved/; this is left unanchored to also catch one
# copied out to another directory for triage during FK-7/FK-8/FK-9 work.
*.dmp

# Editor / OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.idea/
.vscode/

/ghidra/
# The on-disk directory is capital-G `Ghidra/` (2.1 GB project database) and it
# matches the lowercase rule above ONLY because this clone has
# core.ignorecase=true. On a case-sensitive clone that silently stops matching,
# so spell the real name out as well.
/Ghidra/

# Python bytecode caches
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# MSYS/Git-Bash crash droppings
*.stackdump

# Locally-generated TLS chain for the redirect (root CA + leaf + PRIVATE KEY).
# NEVER track these. server/internal/tlscert EnsureCert() generates them on first
# run and REUSES whatever is already on disk, and launch-redirect.ps1 appends
# certs/root.crt to the game's cacert.pem — which is the client's GENERAL CA
# bundle, not a per-host pin. So a committed root.crt/server.key would make every
# self-hoster who starts ags directly (rather than via the launcher, which wipes
# this dir first) install a CA whose private key is public into their trust store.
# The certs are not machine-specific and a shared one would "work"; that is exactly
# why this is easy to get wrong. Nothing needs to be created by hand — EnsureCert
# does os.MkdirAll and generates a fresh 10-year chain when the dir is empty.
/certs/
# ...and server/certs/, which is where the chain actually lands on the documented
# manual recipe: main.go:43's -certs flag defaults to the CWD-relative "certs"
# and ags is normally started with cwd=server/. The launcher passes an absolute
# -certs and so writes the root copy; a hand-started ags writes this one. The
# rule above was anchored to the root and therefore never covered it — which is
# how server/certs/server.key ended up tracked across five commits. Untracking
# is NOT remediation for that key; rotate the chain.
/server/certs/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime output (added after a three-area audit, 2026-08-10). Each rule below
# is anchored to a writer in the tree and was checked against the tracked set
# with `git check-ignore`. docs/ is this project's evidence store, so the rules
# here are deliberately narrow: none of them reaches a .md, a session write-up,
# or a per-run evidence corpus. Do not "tidy" them into wildcards.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# FK-7 A/B: the per-run CLIENT logs only. configs/fk7-ab-run.ps1 copies the
# game's whole Loki.log into docs/fk7ab/<label>/ on every run — 93 files,
# 1.89 GB, six of them over GitHub's 100 MB hard push limit. The stage.log /
# launch.log / marker snapshots that sit beside them in the same directories are
# KEPT on purpose: they are the evidence index behind the Fisher p = 7e-8 result,
# and the analysis lives in docs/s112-fk7-ab-results.md. These 93 are untracked
# already; shedding them from history is a separate filter-repo pass.
/docs/fk7ab/**/Loki.log

# Shim runtime transcripts. Every native shim opens its own docs/<name>-marker.txt
# with CREATE_ALWAYS in DllMain and truncates it once per injection (FK-25), and
# the default launch injects six shims. Anchored to depth 1 DELIBERATELY:
# docs/fk7ab/<label>/tutorial-launch-marker.txt is the archived per-run copy and
# must stay tracked, so never broaden this to `*-marker.txt` or `docs/**/`.
# docs/tutorial-launch-marker.PRE-WPROBE.txt is spared by its suffix.
/docs/*-marker.txt
# ...except the VEH crash-callstack capture (scan_on_enum_veh.cpp:82) — one-shot
# forensics from a crash that may not reproduce, not a regenerable heartbeat.
!/docs/veh-crash-marker.txt

# Shim SEH crash sinks — enumerated, not globbed. A `/docs/*-crash.txt` glob also
# swallows docs/session-39-menu-crash.txt (285 lines of hand-written narrative
# plus a retraction block) and would silently catch any future docs/<fk>-crash.txt
# prose. These are the closed set declared as kCrashPath in tools/sigbypass-mod.
/docs/catalog-ready-fix-crash.txt
/docs/catalog-store-fix-crash.txt
/docs/catalog-pick-fix-crash.txt
/docs/mainmenu-refresh-crash.txt
/docs/mainmenu-refresh-pi*-crash.txt

# Start-Process stderr sinks (launch-redirect.ps1's "$watchOut.err"), truncated
# on every -Hook launch and never yet non-empty. A glob rather than the literal
# path because the name is derived from $watchOut.
/docs/*.out.log.err

# configs/phase0-server.ps1 passes -abslog=<this> and DELETES it before every
# run, so it is ephemeral by its own design. Do NOT broaden to phase0-server*.log
# — the docs/ds-server-backup-* series next door is tracked evidence.
/docs/phase0-server.log

# Two `dotnet run` console captures from the extractor (MSB3246 warnings and a
# Paks/Out path echo). Named exactly rather than globbed: docs/*.log is this
# repo's primary evidence medium (~300 tracked files, incl.
# docs/fk11-live-result-20260809.log) and a family-wide ban there would silently
# drop a future cited capture.
/docs/bpdump-discover.log
/docs/bpdump-style.log

# MSVC compile/link byproducts. tools/sigbypass-mod/.gitignore already declares
# these junk for one directory; hoisting them means the next C++ tool dir is
# covered without a fresh nested file. tools/inject/ never had one, which is why
# 11 of these are tracked there today.
*.exp
*.lib
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.obj
# tools/inject/canary/ deliberately tracks the artifacts of the closed
# "packer eats C++ exception unwinding" experiment. Keep the door open for an
# .obj landing beside them rather than making it silently un-addable.
!/tools/inject/canary/*.obj

# Compiled shims. Source is the deliverable: tools/sigbypass-mod/.gitignore
# states the policy — a stale committed .dll that silently disagrees with its
# source is worse than no .dll at all — and .text sha256 identity is enforced by
# verify_dll.py against locally-built binaries, not by git. Scoped to tools/** so
# it cannot reach the vendored redistributables under Output/.
/tools/**/*.dll

# Build-output directories under tools/. The build/ rule is ONE level deep on
# purpose: a `tools/**/build/` also reaches tools/asdump/out/<Package>/, whose
# directory names come from the GAME's script packages and are re-emitted on
# every dump — a package named `build` would silently drop tracked RE output.
/tools/*/build/
/tools/**/obj/

# Ad-hoc `2> build_err.txt` compiler spew.
/tools/**/build_err.txt

# FModel's own program directory — 18.25 MB of third-party vgmstream / Oodle /
# Detex redistributables plus a 5.85 MB vgmstream-win.zip and an imgui layout
# dropping. CUE4Parse re-downloads them on demand; Output/Logs records it doing
# exactly that. The three text files in there are upstream vgmstream's own
# README/USAGE/COPYING, not project-authored.
/Output/.data/
# Extractor asset exports — regenerable from the paks. The .json is byte-identical
# to docs/exports/WBP_UI_MissionModalCategory.json, which is the copy the docs cite.
/Output/Exports/
# NOTE: deliberately NOT a blanket /Output/. Output/Logs/FModel-Log-2026-06-29.log
# is cited by name in docs/ignorance-map-s101.md:1316 as the evidence artifact for
# ignorance-map item D4.

# S114 exec-surface analysis cache. 119 MB, and every byte is DERIVED: text_union.bin
# is a .text union rebuilt from dumps/ on demand, text_cov.bin its coverage bitmap,
# thunk_callhist.pkl a memoised disassembly pass. Regenerated automatically by
# tools/re/{exec_surface_probe,exec_chain_grade,callers_of}.py, which own the path.
/tools/re/.exec_surface_cache/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Per-run launch/capture artifacts. EVIDENCE for one sitting, not source.
#
# These were committed once by accident (2779f81, 618,258 insertions across 66 files —
# a 230k-line relaunch.out.log, capture/loki snapshots, and a whole scratchpad run dir)
# and must not be again. Back them up under docs/ as usual; git just won't track them.
#
# Deliberately NARROW. Do not broaden to docs/*.log or /scratchpad/ — both hold files that
# are legitimately tracked: the ds-server-*/ds-client-*/fk11-live-result-* log families,
# docs/relaunch-loop.log and docs/relaunch-{normal-,}s52*.out.log (S52 evidence), and
# scratchpad/{stub_recheck*,decode_*}.py (the S115 keepers the ignorance map cites).
# Note docs/loki.log.* matches only the snapshot family — NOT docs/lokiassetmanager-*.md.
/docs/capture.log.*
/docs/loki.log.*
/docs/loki-extract.*
/docs/relaunch.out.log
/docs/relaunch.err.log
/docs/relaunch2.out.log
/docs/relaunch2.err.log
/docs/fk17-relaunch.out.log
/docs/missioninfo-clean-run.out.log
/docs/cold21.out.log
/docs/coldcatalog.out.log
/docs/defaultlaunch.out.log
/scratchpad/s118/
/scratchpad/s118-*
/scratchpad/s118_*

# Per-launch console sinks for the launcher's three helper processes. Truncated or
# overwritten on EVERY launch by their writers:
#   docs/crashwatch.out.log     <- configs/launch-redirect.ps1:341   (usmapdump crashwatch)
#   docs/inject-watch.out.log   <- configs/launch-redirect.ps1:426   ($watchOut, `inject watch`)
#   docs/inject-secondaries.log <- configs/inject-secondaries.ps1:48
#
# They churned across 11-14 commits apiece while never carrying curated evidence.
#
# ⚠ THEY *ARE* CITED — and that is precisely the argument for untracking them, not
# against it. docs/next-session-prompt-s121.md:71 cites this file's content as [M]
# ("pid 81028, 50 ms poll"). That content is ALREADY UNRECOVERABLE: the working copy
# was overwritten by a later launch, and `git log -S 81028 -- docs/crashwatch.out.log`
# returns NOTHING, so it was never committed in the first place. Tracking a file that
# its writer truncates every run preserves whatever the last committer happened to
# hold, not the run being cited — an evidence trail in appearance only.
# ⇒ When one of these matters, COPY IT under a run-specific name (the fk7ab/<label>/
# and capture-s121-* families are how that is done here) and commit the copy.
# History is unaffected: every version ever committed stays reachable by `git show`.
#
# Deliberately three literal paths. Do NOT broaden to /docs/*.out.log — that also
# swallows docs/abstract-run.out.log, docs/relaunch-*.out.log and the rest of the
# tracked evidence families this file already warns about twice.
/docs/crashwatch.out.log
/docs/inject-watch.out.log
/docs/inject-secondaries.log

# S150 Flight 2 raw capture archives (large; kept locally, never tracked)
docs/s150-retirement-*/capture-archive/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Individual files that hit or exceeded GitHub's 100 MB per-file hard push limit.
#
# These sit in commit 38d96d9 (S139) and are the reason `git push origin dedicated-server-stub`
# is rejected until history is rewritten (git-lfs migrate or git-filter-repo). Removing them
# from HEAD in a new commit does NOT unblock the push -- the blob objects stay reachable via
# 38d96d9's tree -- but this .gitignore entry AND the pre-commit hook at configs/git-hooks/
# ensure they cannot be re-added by accident before or after a rewrite.
#
# Regeneration: capture-emote-attempt1.log is the raw docs/capture.log from one live run and
# can be reproduced by re-running the emote sweep with ags's capture on. LVL_Skylands_WP.json
# is a whole-map extractor dump (CUE4Parse), reproducible by re-running the extractor. The
# CONCLUSIONS drawn from both are already in the smaller sibling summary files that stay
# tracked (SUMMARY-NUMBERS.txt beside the log; the smaller LVL_Training.json etc. beside the
# map dump), and in CLAUDE.md's emotes / drop-phase blocks.
#
# Rule: any single blob >= ~100 MB is rejected by GitHub. Prefer LFS for anything that MUST
# stay tracked at that size; prefer .gitignore + a run-specific summary file for evidence.
/scratchpad/s133/evidence/capture-emote-attempt1.log
/scratchpad/s134/laneb/mapdumps/LVL_Skylands_WP.json
